{"nope":{"id":"56c6b745-d460-4197-9bea-37464b055859","word":"nope","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"informal \"no\"","word":"nem"}],"pos":"particle","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"\"Is my son here, Clarence?\" asked Roger Oakley. \"Nope. The whistle ain't blowed yet.\"","ref":"1856, Sidney George Fisher, Charles Edward Fisher, Kanzas and the Constitution, page 97:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[49,53]],"id":"770bb64e-85d5-4f69-a82b-047ade20cc41"},{"text":"\"No,\" from Tom, ending the word with so decided a pressure of the lips that it sounded like \"nope.\"","ref":"1880, R. Foli, Ill weeds, page 319:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[93,97]],"id":"0b7973f2-29cf-46d2-83d3-15836002936d"},{"text":"“Aunt Kat? And was Aunt Kat your only relation? Have you no father nor mother?” “Nope. Never had none ‘cept Aunt Kat. Her hull name was Katrina. She wuz Dutch she wuz.\"","ref":"1890, Werner's Readings and Recitations, E.S. Werner, page 50:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[81,85]],"id":"2e6bbcdf-c56e-408a-9ee0-5736416d8487"},{"text":"1: I will not dishonour my country's speech by leaving off the last syllables of words, 2: I will say a good American \"yes\" and \"no\" in place of an Indian grunt \"um-hum\" and \"nup-um\" or a foreign \"ya\" or \"yeh\" and \"nope\"[…]","ref":"c. 1930, The Detroit Educational Bulletin, Detroit (Michigan) Board of Education, page 13:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[215,219]],"id":"e9568116-1174-43f5-9587-23af2696e98e"},{"text":"Nope. Don't know as I do.","ref":"2006, Charlotte Hudson Ewing, Red Land, AuthorHouse, →ISBN, page 54:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4]],"id":"a3a9be2c-4fc1-41bc-b85e-7d1b86313d0d"}],"categories":["English informal terms","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["No","no"]],"raw_glosses":["(informal, often emphatic) No."],"glosses":["No."],"tags":["emphatic","informal","often"],"id":"3fc2f3f2-a32e-44e1-80fb-a3873365eee1"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"no problem":{"id":"74de75b1-5b77-4632-9b05-d29f65f42713","word":"no problem","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"it does not pose a problem","word":"sem problemas"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"no thanks or apology is necessary","word":"de nada"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"no thanks or apology is necessary","word":"não há de quê"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"no thanks or apology is necessary","word":"sem problema"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"no thanks or apology is necessary","word":"sem grilo"}],"pos":"intj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Porter, can you help me with my bags? — No problem, sir.","id":"2bd8e5cb-3a70-4c81-8c6e-da5665abe735"}],"links":[["Certainly","certainly"],["sure","sure"]],"glosses":["Certainly, sure (said when granting a request)."],"id":"e1d5f249-f85e-485d-a1af-fae4034c8e59"},{"examples":[{"text":"Thank you. — No problem.","bold_text_offsets":[[13,23]],"type":"example","id":"925ce890-73ac-489b-a022-c43171eb0c29"}],"links":[["thanks","thanks"],["necessary","necessary"],["you're welcome","you're welcome"]],"glosses":["No thanks are necessary; you're welcome (said in response to an expression of gratitude)."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"d393290b-aecf-4740-85d1-ba91a13e83a5"},{"examples":[{"text":"I'm sorry. — No problem.","bold_text_offsets":[[13,23]],"type":"example","id":"0f83a404-bb05-4527-af94-cc03f16b4374"}],"links":[["apology","apology"],["necessary","necessary"]],"glosses":["No apology is necessary; think nothing of it (said in response to an expression of regret)."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"54115c8b-9d2e-4416-abcb-ffdafca3a5d8"}],"related":[{"tags":["clipping"],"word":"no prob"},{"word":"no problemo"},{"tags":["Internet"],"word":"NP"}],"synonyms":